	(text "10.     GENERAL CABLE ASSEMBLY REQUIREMENTS:\n  10.1.   FABRICATE CABLES TO THE CONNECTOR, CONTACT, CONDUCTOR SIZE, AND PINOUT\n            REQUIREMENTS SHOWN ON THIS DRAWING.\n  10.2.   USE STRANDED COPPER CONDUCTORS. CONDUCTOR INSULATION SHALL BE UNDAMAGED\n            AND SUITABLE FOR THE INTENDED TERMINAL AND HARNESS APPLICATION.\n  10.3.   CRIMP TERMINALS USING A TOOL SUITABLE FOR THE SPECIFIED CONTACT AND\n            CONDUCTOR SIZE. DO NOT SOLDER CRIMP TERMINALS UNLESS SPECIFICALLY\n            DIRECTED.\n  10.4.   TERMINALS SHALL BE FULLY SEATED AND RETAINED IN THEIR CONNECTOR HOUSINGS.\n            PERFORM A LIGHT PULL CHECK AFTER ASSEMBLY.\n  10.5.   PROVIDE ADEQUATE STRAIN RELIEF AT CONNECTORS, SPLICES, AND CABLE BREAKOUTS.\n            LOADS SHALL NOT BE CARRIED BY INDIVIDUAL TERMINALS OR CONDUCTORS.\n  10.6.   INSULATE ALL SPLICES, UNUSED CONDUCTORS, DRAIN WIRES, AND EXPOSED\n            CONDUCTIVE MATERIAL USING HEAT SHRINK OR EQUIVALENT INSULATION.\n  10.7.   ROUTE AND SECURE CONDUCTORS TO PREVENT CHAFING, SHARP BENDS, EXCESSIVE\n            TENSION, AND INTERFERENCE WITH MOVING PARTS.\n  10.8.   CABLE LENGTH SHALL BE SUFFICIENT FOR INSTALLATION AND SERVICE WITHOUT\n            PLACING TENSION ON CONNECTORS. AVOID EXCESSIVE UNSECURED SLACK.\n  10.9.   IDENTIFY CABLES AND CONNECTORS AS REQUIRED TO SUPPORT INSTALLATION,\n            TROUBLESHOOTING, AND CORRECT MATING.\n  10.10.  VERIFY CONTINUITY, PIN-TO-PIN WIRING, AND ABSENCE OF UNINTENDED SHORTS BEFORE\n            INSTALLATION.\n  10.11.  WHERE REQUIREMENTS IN A CABLE-SPECIFIC NOTE CONFLICT WITH THESE GENERAL\n            REQUIREMENTS, THE CABLE-SPECIFIC REQUIREMENT SHALL GOVERN.\n11.     RS485 DATA RUN REQUIREMENTS\n  11.1.   DATA CONDUCTORS A AND B SHALL BE STRANDED COPPER CONDUCTORS, TWISTED AS A\n            SHIELDED PAIR (STP). THE SHIELD SHALL NOT BE USED AS BUS GND, POWER RETURN,\n            OR A CURRENT-CARRYING CONDUCTOR.\n  11.2.   MAINTAIN SHIELD CONTINUITY THROUGH THE COMPLETE RS485 DATA RUN, INCLUDING\n            ALL INTERMEDIATE CABLE, BULKHEAD, OR HARNESS CONNECTIONS.\n  11.3.   THE SHIELD SHALL BE BONDED TO GND ONLY AT THE OWNING ABSIS BUS MASTER J6\n            CONNECTION. DO NOT BOND THE SHIELD TO BUS GND, PCB GND, CHASSIS, OR\n            STRUCTURE AT INTERMEDIATE CONNECTIONS OR AT THE FAR END OF THE DATA RUN.\n  11.4.   THE FAR END OF THE SHIELD SHALL BE INSULATED AND LEFT UNBONDED.\n  11.5.   INSULATE AND STRAIN-RELIEVE ALL SHIELD/DRAIN SPLICES, PIGTAILS, AND\n            TERMINATIONS. KEEP EXPOSED DRAIN CONDUCTORS AND PIGTAILS AS SHORT AS\n            PRACTICAL.\n  11.6.   WHERE A CABLE DRAIN CONDUCTOR IS NOT COMPATIBLE WITH THE REQUIRED CRIMP\n            CONTACT, USE AN INSULATED SPLICE TO A COMPATIBLE STRANDED PIGTAIL. DO NOT\n            FORCE AN OVERSIZED CONDUCTOR OR MULTIPLE DRAIN CONDUCTORS INTO A SINGLE\n            CRIMP CONTACT.\n  11.7.   EACH ABSIS BUS MASTER RS485 SEGMENT SHALL HAVE A SEPARATE DETACHABLE\n            SHIELD-DRAIN CONNECTION ASSOCIATED WITH ITS J2, J3, OR J4 BUS CABLE.\n  11.8.   CONNECT ABSIS BUS MASTER J6 TO A SHORT, SECURED LEAD AND INSULATED FAN-OUT\n            PROVIDING ONE DRAIN CONNECTION FOR EACH RS485 SEGMENT. REMOVAL OF AN\n            RS485 BUS CABLE SHALL NOT REQUIRE LOOSENING OR REMOVING THE J6 SCREW\n            CONNECTION.\n  11.9.   MASTER-SIDE FIXED DRAIN CONNECTOR SHALL USE:\n          11.9.1. SMP-02V-BC HOUSING\n          11.9.2. 1X SHF-001T-0.8BS FEMALE CONTACT\n          11.9.3. POPULATE CAVITY 1 ONLY.\n          11.9.4. CAVITY 2 SHALL CONTAIN NO CONTACT OR CONDUCTOR.\n  11.10.  REMOVABLE CABLE-SIDE DRAIN CONNECTOR SHALL USE:\n          11.10.1. SMR-02V-B HOUSING\n          11.10.2. 1X SYM-001T-P0.6(N) MALE CONTACT\n          11.10.3. POPULATE CAVITY 1 ONLY.\n          11.10.4. CAVITY 2 SHALL CONTAIN NO CONTACT OR CONDUCTOR.\n  11.11.  VERIFY CAVITY NUMBERING FROM THE CONNECTOR MATING-FACE VIEW. DO NOT\n            DETERMINE CAVITY NUMBER FROM WIRE-ENTRY ORIENTATION ALONE.\n  11.12.  LABEL BOTH HALVES OF EACH DRAIN CONNECTOR WITH THE ASSOCIATED RS485\n            SEGMENT AND ROUTE AND SECURE THE DRAIN CONNECTOR WITH ITS ASSOCIATED BUS\n            CABLE.\n  11.13.  THE TWO-POSITION JST SM HOUSING IS NOT MECHANICALLY KEYED TO THIS\n            APPLICATION. ROUTE, RESTRAIN, AND IDENTIFY DRAIN CONNECTORS TO PREVENT\n            CONNECTION TO OTHER TWO-POSITION JST SM CIRCUITS.\n  11.14.  VERIFY CORRECT PIN-TO-PIN CONTINUITY OF ALL RS485 BUS CONDUCTORS AND\n            CONTINUITY OF THE SHIELD THROUGH THE COMPLETE DATA RUN.\n  11.15.  WITH THE MASTER-END DRAIN CONNECTION DISCONNECTED, VERIFY THE SHIELD IS\n            ISOLATED FROM BUS GND, PCB GND, CHASSIS, AND STRUCTURE.\n  11.16.  VERIFY CAVITY 1 IS POPULATED AND CAVITY 2 IS EMPTY ON BOTH HALVES OF EACH\n            TWO-POSITION JST SM DRAIN CONNECTION.\n  11.17.  VERIFY CRIMP-CONTACT RETENTION, INSULATION, STRAIN RELIEF, AND CABLE\n            RESTRAINT.\n  11.18.  AFTER ASSEMBLY, VERIFY NORMAL RS485 COMMUNICATION WITH THE INTENDED BUS\n            MASTER, REPRESENTATIVE NODES, AND REPRESENTATIVE SWITCHED ELECTRICAL\n            LOADS OPERATING."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
